idden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t<\/span>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/summary>\n\t\t\t\t<div role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"e-n-accordion-item-1730\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-225e9af e-con-full e-flex wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"225e9af\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-688bd7f9 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"688bd7f9\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For most common strains or stress-related issues, you should see significant improvement within one to two weeks of starting conservative treatment. If the pain lasts longer than three months, we classify it as chronic, and we may need a more detailed plan.<\/span><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<details id=\"e-n-accordion-item-1731\" class=\"e-n-accordion-item\" >\n\t\t\t\t<summary class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title\" data-accordion-index=\"2\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"e-n-accordion-item-1731\" >\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-header'><div class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title-text\"> Can my neck pain be caused by how I sleep? <\/div><\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-icon'>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-opened' ><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-closed'><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t<\/span>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/summary>\n\t\t\t\t<div role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"e-n-accordion-item-1731\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-32276ac0 e-con-full e-flex wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"32276ac0\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-684b609c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"684b609c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Absolutely. Sleeping on your stomach with your head turned to the side for eight hours puts a massive strain on the cervical joints. I recommend sleeping on your side or back with a pillow that keeps your ears aligned with your shoulders.<\/span><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<details id=\"e-n-accordion-item-1732\" class=\"e-n-accordion-item\" >\n\t\t\t\t<summary class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title\" data-accordion-index=\"3\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"e-n-accordion-item-1732\" >\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-header'><div class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title-text\"> What are the most common reasons for neck and shoulder pain in Dubai? <\/div><\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-icon'>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-opened' ><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-closed'><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t<\/span>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/summary>\n\t\t\t\t<div role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"e-n-accordion-item-1732\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-aa61489 e-con-full e-flex wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"aa61489\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-59d809ba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"59d809ba\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In my experience, &#8220;Tech-Neck&#8221; from office work and muscle spasms caused by cold AC vents are the top two local culprits. Stress also plays a major role in the tension we see in the upper back.<\/span><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<details id=\"e-n-accordion-item-1733\" class=\"e-n-accordion-item\" >\n\t\t\t\t<summary class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title\" data-accordion-index=\"4\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"e-n-accordion-item-1733\" >\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-header'><div class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title-text\"> When is neck pain considered an emergency? <\/div><\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-icon'>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-opened' ><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-closed'><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t<\/span>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/summary>\n\t\t\t\t<div role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"e-n-accordion-item-1733\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-162cc617 e-flex e-con-boxed wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"162cc617\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-40a04c7e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"40a04c7e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Please seek immediate care if your pain follows a serious accident, if you lose control of your bladder or bowels, or if you feel a sudden, profound weakness in your arms or legs.<\/span><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/details>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4bd66de8 e-flex e-con-boxed wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"4bd66de8\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4845dc9a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"4845dc9a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Conclusion: Your Journey Back to Wellness<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-185aa60b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"185aa60b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the end of the day, my greatest reward is seeing a patient return to my office with a smile, telling me they played their first full game of golf in months or that they finally slept through the night without waking up in pain.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Identifying the <\/span>reasons for neck and shoulder pain<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a collaborative journey. We will work together, step by step, to ensure your recovery is smooth and lasting. Don&#8217;t let &#8220;just an ache&#8221; turn into a chronic burden. Let&#8217;s address it today with the care and expertise you deserve.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Would you like to take the first step toward a pain-free life?<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br \/><\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/contact\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b>Book an appointment with Dr. Usama Saleh today<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and join our family of healthy, active patients.<\/span><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-50deea40 e-flex e-con-boxed wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"50deea40\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-22e5cf9f elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"22e5cf9f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h3 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">references<\/h3>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7015acc6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"7015acc6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<ol><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/orthoinfo.aaos.org\/en\/diseases--conditions\/neck-pain\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons (AAOS) on Neck Pain<\/span><\/a><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.mayoclinic.org\/diseases-conditions\/neck-pain\/symptoms-causes\/syc-20375581\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mayo Clinic &#8211; Neck Pain Causes<\/span><\/a><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.google.com\/search?q=https:\/\/my.clevelandclinic.org\/health\/diseases\/21171-neck-pain\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cleveland Clinic &#8211; Cervicalgia (Neck Pain)<\/span><\/a><\/li><\/ol>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>If you are reading this, perhaps you woke up today feeling a heavy tightness across your shoulders, or maybe a sharp, nagging ache in your neck made it difficult to drive your children to school or focus on your work here in Dubai. You might now be wondering what are the reasons for neck and shoulder pain I&#8217;m experiencing. I want you to know one thing immediately: You are not alone, and you are in the right place. In my years as an orthopedic specialist, I have sat across from thousands of neighbors, friends, and patients who felt frustrated by persistent discomfort. My philosophy at the Dr. Usama Saleh clinic is simple: You are family. I don\u2019t just see a case of cervicalgia; I see a person who wants to get back to their active life, their family gatherings, and their professional goals without being held back by pain. Understanding the reasons for neck and shoulder pain is the first step toward reclaiming your well-being. The neck and shoulders are more than just bone and muscle; they are the bridge between your mind and your body. When that bridge is under stress, your whole quality of life can feel the impact. Common reasons for neck and shoulder pain. The human head weighs about 5 kilograms. roughly the weight of a heavy bowling ball. Your neck, or the cervical spine, is responsible for balancing that weight while allowing you to rotate, tilt, and look at the world around you. Because the nerves that travel to your arms and shoulders originate in your neck, it is very common for a problem in one area to be felt in the other. 1. The Modern Tech-Neck and Physical Strain One of the most frequent reasons for neck and shoulder pain I see in my Dubai practice is related to our modern lifestyle. Whether you are an executive in DIFC hunched over a laptop for ten hours a day or someone constantly looking down at a smartphone, your neck muscles are working overtime. This &#8220;forward head posture&#8221; strains the ligaments and creates a persistent, dull ache that eventually radiates into the shoulder blades. 2. The Natural Process of Aging (Wear and Tear) As we get older, our bodies change. just like a well-loved home that needs a little extra maintenance. Osteoarthritis: The smooth cartilage between your joints can wear down over time, leading to stiffness. Degenerative Disk Disease: The cushions (disks) between your vertebrae lose water as you age, bringing the bones closer together and causing irritation. Bone Spurs: Sometimes, the body tries to heal itself by growing extra bone, which can unfortunately press on sensitive nerves. 3. Injuries and Whiplash Dubai is a city on the move, and unfortunately, minor traffic accidents or sports injuries (like a fall during a weekend football match or a sudden jerk during Padel) can cause whiplash. This occurs when the head is snapped forward and back, overstretching the soft tissues. Recognizing the Symptoms: What Is Your Body Telling You? When we meet in my office, I will ask you to describe your pain as if you were talking to a brother. Is it a zap, a burn, or a heavy weight? Recognizing these symptoms helps us narrow down the reasons for neck and shoulder pain specific to your body. Axial Pain: This is felt primarily in the neck itself. It might feel like a kink that makes it hard to turn your head to check your blind spot while driving. Radicular Pain: This is the shooting sensation. It travels from the neck, over the shoulder, and sometimes all the way down to the fingers. Numbness and Tingling: Often described as pins and needles, this usually suggests that a nerve is being slightly squeezed or pinched. Muscle Spasms: Your body\u2019s way of trying to protect an injured area by tightening the muscles into a hard, painful knot. Read also: shoulder blade pain treatment with Dr. Usama Saleh Dr. Usama\u2019s Diagnostic Pathway: A Compassionate Approach I believe that a good doctor should be a great detective. We don&#8217;t just jump to conclusions; we listen to the clues your body provides. The Personal Conversation (Medical History) I want to hear about your daily routine. Do you sit at a desk? Do you carry a heavy laptop bag over one shoulder? Have you had any recent falls? Understanding your lifestyle story is often more revealing than a scan. The Gentle Physical Exam I will observe how you move, check your posture, and feel the muscles of your neck and upper back. I look for trigger points or areas of tenderness that tell me which structures are under duress. Advanced Imaging (Only When Necessary) In the spirit of being a responsible doctor, I don\u2019t order tests unless they truly add value to your recovery. X-Rays: To look at the alignment of your bones and check for signs of arthritis. MRI: The gold standard for seeing &#8220;soft tissues&#8221; like herniated disks or pinched nerves. CT Scans: Best for looking at bone spurs or complex bone structures. Visit my official website now &#8211; usamasaleh.com &#8211; and discover the medical treatments and services I offer, as well as my clients&#8217; review about these services. Treatment Options for neck and shoulder pain. The good news is that most reasons for neck and shoulder pain do not require surgery. At the Dr. Usama Saleh clinic, we prioritize the most gentle, effective treatments first. Conservative and Home Remedies Temperature Therapy: A warm shower or heating pad can loosen tight muscles, while an ice pack is wonderful for reducing inflammation after a sudden strain. Ergonomic Adjustments: We will talk about your desk setup. Raising your monitor to eye level can be life-changing. Activity Modification: Sometimes, the body just needs a &#8220;time-out&#8221; from the activity that caused the strain. Professional Therapy Physical Therapy: I work closely with wonderful therapists who can teach you specific exercises to strengthen your &#8220;back extensor&#8221; muscles, pulling your shoulders back into their natural, healthy position.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":9987,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"elementor_theme","categories":[12],"tags":[85,88,89,87,86],"class_list":["post-10475","blogs","type-blogs","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-shoulder","tag-cervical-health","tag-ergonomics","tag-neck-and-shoulder-doctor","tag-orthopedic-care","tag-tech-neck"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/blogs\/10475","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/blogs"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/blogs"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=10475"}],"version-history":[{"count":10,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/blogs\/10475\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":10603,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/blogs\/10475\/revisions\/10603"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/9987"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=10475"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https: